Topics to remember:
VARIABLE TYPES:
  CHAR-
    a char is a variable that stores single character enclosed within single quotes 
  STRING-
    a string tyoe is a special type of variable that consists of multiple characters and is nclosed within double quotes
  CONSTANTS-
    a constant is a special type of variable that cannot be changed once it is initialised and to declare a constant we use the keyword final followed by the variable type
    and variable name

VARIABLE NAMING:
   USE CAMELCASE- variable naming should start with a lowercase then upper case
   CONSTANT NAME- is written in uppercase

GENERAL RULES:
  1. name should start with a letter  or underscore, dollar sign 
  2. it should not start with a number 

TYPE CASTING:
process of converting a value from one data type to another. in java we can connvert it to double to int, int to double etc

It is of two types-
1. IMPLICIT CASTING ( automatic)-  int to double 
   int number=5;
   double decimal=number; // now decimal=5.0
2. EXPLICIT CASTING (manual)- double to int
   double decimal=9.7;
   int number=(int)decimal;//here number=9 
3. CONVERTION OF NUMBERS AND BOOLEAN TO STRING-
    It is also possible to convert number and booleans to string and vice versa. To convert a value to string we can use the String.valueOf() function
    int number1 = 789;
    double number2 = 789;
    boolean isValid = true;
    String text1 = String.valueOf(number1); // becomes "789"
    String text2 = String.valueOf(number2); // becomes "789.0"
    String text3 = String.valueOf(isValid); // becomes "true"
4.STRING TO INTEGER-
    String numberText = "123";
    int number = Integer.parseInt(numberText);    // becomes 123
5.STRING TO DOUBLE-
    String decimalText = "45.67";
    double decimal = Double.parseDouble(decimalText);    // becomes 45.67
6.STRING TO BOOLEAN
    String boolText = "true";
    boolean bool = Boolean.parseBoolean(boolText); // becomes true
